   <h3> Inner-Guild Dispute Procedures</h3>
   <p>
   
<p>Primary rule: Praise in public, criticize in private
<p>If two or more members within the guild have a conflict or disagreement, they 
  must resolve the dispute as follows: 
<ol>
 <li>Take all disputes out of /guild chat.  Arguments in guild chat will not be tolerated.  It annoys people and damages morale.  The two members that are in dispute <u>must</u> discuss the issue in private tells.
  <li>If the two individuals are unable to resolve the issue between them on their 
    own, they may contact a Bone Guard member via private tells to help with the 
    situation. The Bone Guard member will attempt to resolve the situation as 
    quickly and as fairly as possible. If a Bone Guard member is not available, 
    a higher ranking member (Blood Knight, Circle of Bones, Warlord) may be contacted, 
    but in that order. 
  <li>If either party is not satisfied with the decision, they can ask that a higher ranking member hear the complaint.  At this point the Bone Guard should contact a superior ranking member and forward the situation to them.
 <li>If a Blood Knight or higher rank refuses to hear the dispute, the Bone Guard's decision stands.
</ol>

It should be STRONGLY noted that all attempts should be made to resolve all disputes 
at the lowest rank possible. The higher ranking members have many things to deal 
with and handling extra disputes not only makes their lives more difficult, but 
it prevents them from focusing on their real duties. 

  </td>
